  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 7.5. Increased capacity of Member States to develop fair and effective labour migration frameworks, institutions and services to protect migrant workers</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">In September 2022, the Uganda Hotels, Food, Tourism, Supermarkets &amp; Allied Workers&apos; Union (HTS-Union) established a Migrant Workers Resource Centre (MRC). The MRC is a one-stop centre for potential, current and returnee migrant workers in Uganda to access information and other support services before departure and upon return. The MRC promotes safe labour migration channels, and provides information on where and how to seek assistance for existing and potential migrant workers.
Between September 2022-June 2023, the MRC handled 139 cases (106 women and 33 men) seeking information on migration.
The MRC also provides information on job placement, standard employment contracts, repatriation of migrants stranded in the Middle East and business opportunities and counselling services.
Sustainability is assured as the MRC is permanently housed at the premises of HTS-Union thus reducing on operational costs. Union dues will be collected from unionized migrant domestic workers and other contributions and support of the other sectors of the union.
An MoU was signed in May 2023 between HTS-Union and Uganda Association of External Recruitment Agencies (UAERA). The MoU aims to advance, promote and protect Uganda migrant workers&apos; rights and dignity through fair recruitment and monitoring. 
The MoU will ease the process of accessing migrant workers and returnee migrant workers and enable the MRC to provide information and support services effectively and in a timely manner  The newly recruited migrant workers as members will be contact references for other migrant workers in the Middle East countries for recruitment purposes. The ILO, with support from the Government of Switzerland, supported the set up and operationalization of the Migrant Workers Resource Centre in September 2022
ILO built capacity of HTS-Union and UAERA to support the development of the MoU.</narrative>
   </description>
